# evm-bench 219, optimised contracts, Fast Ligerito profile (table-driven tensor algebra, subspace table with mu-folded consistency, discharge v2 with closed-form link families, per-claim 8-bit tables, piecewise segment hashing, row loop in Yul)
# 2026-09-16, M4 Max, revm 43.0.2 under Osaka rules with the gas cap, block limit and code-size limit lifted; one process, quiet machine.
# The lift was read from a cache proved earlier the same day by this binary (the baseline run proved it in 13.38 s); the native verifier re-accepts it before metering.
# The discharge ran as keccakPart, one rows call over the whole stream, then finish; the stream is not split into 2^24-gas transactions, so the transaction count is a lower bound.
# 'intrinsic' is 21,000 plus standard calldata pricing (4 per zero byte, 16 per nonzero); the EIP-7623 floor never binds here.

